<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2025- exam 42</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2025- EXAM 42 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 6/26<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 01 phút 31 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T08:00:06.294Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Seven Testing Principles is a number of testing principles have been suggested over the past 40 years and offer general guidelines common for all testing. Which one of the following descriptions about seven testing principles is FALSE?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testing everything is not feasible except for trivial cases. Instead of exhaustive testing, risk analysis and priorities should be used to focus testing efforts. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing effort shall be focused proportionally to the expected and later observed defect density of modules.</div><div class="opt ">c. Finding and fixing defects does not help if the system built is unusable and does not fulfill the user's needs and expectations.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Testing can show that defects are present, and can prove that there are no defects [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.3 Hỏi nguyên lý nào sai? Chú ý vào D có đoạn " can prove that there are no defects" cái này sai với lý thuyết là Test ko chứng minh đc điều gì</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">During test analysis, the test basis documentation is analyzed in order to determine what to test, i.e., to identify the test conditions. How does a test condition relate to a test case?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A test condition is the output from a test case [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. A test case creates test conditions</div><div class="opt ">c. A test condition defines the test case</div><div class="opt correct">d. A test case tests a test condition [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1. mối quan hệ của test case và test condition. Test case là để kiểm tra cho 1 test condition hoặc nói ngược lại thì 1 test condition có thể đc kiểm tra bởi 1 đến nhiều TC.</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">The formality of a review process is related to factors such as the maturity of the development process, any legal or regulatory requirements or the need for an audit trail. The followings details about the main phases of a formal review. Which is NOT correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Planning: defining the review criteria and selecting the personnel [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Kick-off: selecting which parts of documents to review [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Rework: fixing defects found and recording updated status of defects</div><div class="opt ">d. Follow-up: checking that defects have been addressed</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2 Review process. Thì Kick-off đang đc ghép sai với 1 task của planning. "selecting which parts of documents to review" là của planning</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Which of document should be prepared prior to test execution?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test condition [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test case [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Test design</div><div class="opt ">d. Test procedures</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Tài liệu cần thiết chuẩn bị trước khi chạy test thường là TC và test data</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Which following description is NOT correct about Unit test should be?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Atomic: Unit tests should be only tested the maintenanced related to it [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Fast: Unit tests should be small and fast so they can provide immediate feedback. It should be possible to run many unit tests in a short period of time</div><div class="opt ">c. Isolated: Unit test should strive to exercise only the specific code for which it was initially</div><div class="opt ">d. Independent: Unit tests should not depend on each other and should avoid dependencies in the production code whenever possible</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Cái này tra trên mạng định nghĩa của Unit test trong dự án Agile: Fast, Independent, Isolated, Automic. Xem định nghĩa nào sai với trên mạng. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/testing/unit-testing-best-practices</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">You are going to be testing a small camera. To keep it simple, there are only two buttons: the power button and the shutter button. The camera will act as an automatic focus and exposure camera when the shutter button is pressed halfway and then stopped for 0.4 seconds before the button press is completed. If the shutter button is simply pressed all the way without stop-ping, the camera will act as a single exposure, infinity focus camera. Given the following state transition diagram, how many rows would its matching state transition table contain that cover 0-switch and 1-switch segments?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 9 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 15 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 18</div><div class="opt ">d. 20</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Chương 4 state transition, điếm 0-switch là TC có 1 giao dịch: 1,2,3,4,5,6, 1-witch là TC có 2 giao dịch điếm từ các trạng thái: A: 12 14 13 B: 35 46 C: 56 D: 64 62 63</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">A remote subsystem developer has delivered a module that decides whether to sound an alarm based on three inputs (a HEAT sensor, a SMOKE sensor, and a user-triggered BUTTON). An alarm should sound if both the HEAT sensor and the SMOKE sensor are triggered, or if the alarm BUTTON is triggered. What is the minimum set of test combinations from the following sets of input values that achieve 100% Decision Condition coverage? 1. HEAT=true, SMOKE=true, BUTTON=false 2. HEAT=true, SMOKE=true, BUTTON=true 3. HEAT=true, SMOKE=false, BUTTON=false 4. HEAT=false, SMOKE=false, BUTTON=true 5. HEAT=false, SMOKE=false, BUTTON=false 6. HEAT=false, SMOKE=true, BUTTON=false</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 3 and 6 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 1 and 4</div><div class="opt ">c. 2, 4, and 6</div><div class="opt correct">d. 2 and 5 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 White box test phần data flow: 100% Decision Condition coverage là đảm bảo cả Conditions và cả Decision đều đc chạy T,F ít nhất 1 lần</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following test techniques would most likely have been able to detect the underlying defect?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedright">a. Decision testing [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Statement testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Checklist-based testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Error guessing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 White box test, search trên mạng theo image tìm từ nested loop để hình dung ra ntn gọi là vòng lặp lồng nhau, ở đây có 3 cái hàm for lồng nhau. Và TH lỗi xảy ra là khi có 1 KH ko có bất cứ giao dịch nào của tháng trước thì hệ thống ko gửi đc email như vậy là chưa test TH F của hàm for. Do đó kỹ thuật cần để tìm lỗi là Decision coverage</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following describes the purpose of dynamic analysis tool?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To enable tests to be executed automaticallv or semi-automatically, using stored inputs and expected outcomes. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. To help with review processes, and may store / communicate checklists and guidelines, comments, and track defects and effort</div><div class="opt ">c. To detennine the differences between expected and actual test results</div><div class="opt correct">d. To find. defects only evident when the software is executing, such as time dependencies or memory-leaks. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1 cái bảng so sánh static testing và dynamic testing, nhớ là dynamic analysis tool là tool phân tích động giúp tìm ra lỗi về memory leak</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following statements describes an exploratory test charter BEST?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Indicating that the tester should take the role of a novice user can be part of an exploratory test charter [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. The test charter is elaborated during the testing session according to test execution results</div><div class="opt ">c. Each exploratory test charter is based on a previously defined list of activities that would be interesting to test</div><div class="opt ">d. Testers use the exploratory test charter during the testing session to define the test oracle</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.2 test exploratory. Chú ý đáp án D nó sai ở "define the test oracle " cái này ko có trong sách. C sai vì câu "based on a previously defined list of activities" Test charter ko dựa vào 1 danh sách các hoạt động đc định nghĩa trước. B sai vì "according to test execution results " ý nó nói là dựa vào kết quả test để khám phá ra test charter cũng ko phải. Chỉ có A đúng dịch là Tester nên đóng vai trò như 1 user để test khám phá theo test charter</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">You are going to be testing a small camera. To keep it simple, there are only two buttons: the power button and the shutter button. The camera will act as an automatic focus and exposure camera when the shutter button is pressed halfway and then stopped for 0.4 seconds before the button press is completed. If the shutter button is simply pressed all the way without stop-ping, the camera will act as a single exposure, infinity focus camera. Given the following state transition diagram, how many rows would its matching state transition table contain?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 10 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 18 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 14</div><div class="opt ">d. 20</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.4 Câu này bảng state table tính cả 0-switch 1- switch và 2-switch</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following is the BEST definition of a waterfall model?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Defining requirements, designing software and testing are done in phases where in each phase a piece of the system is added [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing is viewed as a separate phase which takes place after development has been completed</div><div class="opt correct">c. A phase in the development process should begin when the previous phase is complete [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Testing is added to development as an increment</div><div class="opt ">e. A phase in the testing process should begin when the previous phase is complete</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> họ chỉ thêm đáp án E thôi nhưng mà E vẫn sai, Test xen kẽ với các hoạt động phát triển</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following terms is used to describe the management of software components comprising an integrated system?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Configuration management [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Incident management</div><div class="opt ">c. Test monitoring</div><div class="opt ">d. Risk management</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> giải thích của họ: Incident management is the collection and processing of incidents raised when errors and defects are discovered. Test monitoring identifies the status of the testing activity on a continuous basis. Risk management identifies, analyses and mitigates risks to the project and the product. Configuration management is concerned with the management of changes to software components and their associated documentation and testware.</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">A product owner says that your role as a tester on an Agile team is to catch all the bugs before the end of each iteration. Which of the following is a testing principle that could be used to respond to FALSE this statement?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Defect clustering [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing shows the presence of defects</div><div class="opt ">c. Absence of error fallac</div><div class="opt correct">d. Root cause analysis [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Câu này mà hỏi nguyên lý nào đúng thì đã trả lời là A rồi, nhưng các bạn đi thi về khẳng định nó hỏi là FALSE, ý là sai với khẳng định định trên. Nên mình chọn D vì D ko phải là nguyên lý của hoạt động test</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is true about Formal Review or Inspection? i. Led by Trained Moderator (not the author). ii. No Pre Meeting Preparations iii. Formal Follow up process. iv. Main objective is to find defects</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. ii is true and i, iii, iv are false [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. i, iii, iv are true and ii is false [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. i, iii, iv are false and ii is true</div><div class="opt ">d. iii is true and I, ii, iv are false</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> nó đang hỏi về hình thức review inspection có đặc điểm gì thì theo sách chương 3 có i, iii, iv đúng</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is not an example of common test metrics?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Percentage of work done in test environment creation [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Average number of expected defects per requirement [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Number of test cases run</div><div class="opt ">d. Deviation from test milestone dates</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> A là metric vì đo về test environment, C là metric của test đo về TC chạy, D là đo về thời gian test bị lệch với plan, Còn B là 1 metrics của dự án, đo chung cho cả dự án chứ ko phải common test metrics ( B là trung bình lỗi mong muốn trên 1 requirement là metric của dự án)</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of minimum Test case to cover all statements and decision coverage of this code?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 2</div><div class="opt correct">c. 3 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 4</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Chỉ cần 3 TC thôi, bạn nên vẽ thêm sơ đồ DO While và thấy rằng chỉ cần 1 TC đi qua hết cả T và F của cái Do while này rồi.</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">To achieve 100% Modified Condition/Decision Coverage (MC/DC) which set of test cases should be used?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedright">a. Cases 3, 5, 6, and 7 [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Cases 1, 2, 3, and 4</div><div class="opt ">c. Cases 2, 4, 6, and 8</div><div class="opt ">d. Cases 1, 3, 5, and 7</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Câu 37 đề automotive exam. đọc đề thì hiểu là MODERATE là cái decision outcome dự vào các điều kiện của 3 biến, hàm của nó là If ((SPEED or STRESS) and ACTIVE) then MODERATE. đi tìm TC để đạt 100% MC/DC</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements about test estimation approaches is CORRECT? (Choose TWO)</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. With the metrics-based approach, estimation needed to assist with planning before the testing starts [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">b. With the expert-based approach, a group of expert users identified by the client recommends the necessary testing budget [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">c. With the expert-based approach, the test leads responsible for the different testing activities predict the expected testing effort [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. With the metrics-based approach, an average of the testing costs recorded from several past projects is used as the testing budget</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> chương 5 estimation, câu này họ sửa đáp án A trong sách về thành đúng rồi chú ý từ Before nên A đúng, C đúng. B sai vì expert user ko phải là thành viên dự án nên ko đưa dc estimation, D sai vì cost và budget ko phải là cái mà ta học của chương 5 ( ở đây chỉ có kỹ thuật estimate test effort thôi)</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following would you NOT expect to see on an incident report from test execution?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Expected results and actual results [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The version(s) of the software under test</div><div class="opt correct">c. The test execution schedule [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Precise steps to reproduce the problem</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.4 defect management. Cái ko cần nhìn thấy trong incident report là đáp án C. schedule</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements CORRECTLY reflects the value of static testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. By introducing reviews, we have found that both the quality of specifications and the time required for development and testing have increased. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Using static testing means we have better control and cheaper defect management due to the ease of removing defects later in the lifecycle.</div><div class="opt ">c. Now that we require the use of static analysis, missed requirements have decreased and communication between testers and developers has improved.</div><div class="opt correct">d. Since we started using static analysis, we find coding defects that might have not been found by performing only dynamic testing. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.1. A sai vì nó bảo "time required for development and testing have increased". B sai vì "cheaper defect management" cái này ko có nói trong sách. C sai vì "use of static analysis, missed requirements have decreased " - phân tích tĩnh bằng tool thì ko tìm đc lỗi về requirement. Còn D là đúng vì static analysis là tool giúp tìm đc lỗi về coding defect cái mà ko tìm đc bởi dynamic testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Some tools are geared more for developer use. For the 5 tools listed, which statement BEST details those for developers i) Performance testing tools. ii) Coverage measurement tools. iii) Test comparators. iv) Dynamic analysis tools. v) Incident management tools.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. i, iii. and iv. are more for developers. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. ii. and iv. are more for developers. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. ii, iii and iv. are more for developers.</div><div class="opt ">d. ii. and iii. are more for developers.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">You are testing a scale system determines shipping rate for the regional web based auto parts distributor. Due to regulations, shipments cannot exceed 100 kg. You want to included boundary value analysis as part of your black-box test design. How many tests will you need to execute to achieve 100% boundary values analysis? [K3] Weight---Shipping cost 1 to 10 kg--
511
